# Unit Tests Required

- Applies to `.cs` source changes.
- Add or update unit tests for every new behavior change, bug fix, or code path added in C# code.
- Treat code as incomplete until tests cover the intended behavior.
- Prefer focused unit tests close to the changed C# logic.
- Include negative and edge-case coverage when behavior has branches.
- If a C# change cannot be unit tested, explicitly state why and propose the nearest automated test level.

## Examples

```text
Code change (.cs): Add input validation for NPC interaction range.
Test change: Add unit tests that verify valid ranges pass and invalid ranges fail.
```
